\sendkeys sends every key pressed and released in the
current pane via OSC to another LiveLily, which receives
them with \fromosc. Messages are sent to port 9050.
It takes two arguments, the IP of the receiving computer
and the number of its pane (counting from 1):

\sendkeys 192.168.1.20 1

The keys are sent to the address /livelily1/press and
/livelily1/release, which is what \fromosc listens to by
default in the first pane of the receiving LiveLily.
The keys are still typed in the local pane as well.
There is no option to stop sending keys.

To send whole lines when they are executed, use
\sendlines.
